look_fors.strong_examples:
- "Time for centers. Each step on my count. One…" &lt;Students stand up&gt; "Two…" &lt;Students push in chairs; a few haven't&gt; "Chairs in." &lt;Those students push in&gt; "Three." &lt;Students move to centers&gt;
- "Which response was stronger? Turn and talk to your partner for 2 minutes." &lt;Students independently turn to known partner and discuss&gt;
- "Ok, four minutes for the do now today." &lt;Students proceed directly into the Do Now with no further direction&gt;

- End-of-week survey: "What's one thing about how we do centers that's working well? What's one thing that's hard?"
- "Before we wrap up, turn and talk: what's one change to our line-up routine that would help us get to specials on time?" &lt;Students discuss and share ideas&gt;
- "I noticed a few of you struggled to get started on the do now today. What would make that easier for you?"
